/* ═══ STRIKE POSITION ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   GENERATED from catalog/edges.js — do not hand-edit.

   A membrane mode (m,n) is excited in proportion to
       J_m(beta_mn * r/a) * cos(m * (theta - theta0))
   at the strike point. Move the stick and the AMPLITUDE VECTOR moves;
   the frequencies and the decay rates do not. That is why two hits in
   different places are the same drum twice and not two drums — and it is
   what per-hit gain jitter cannot imitate, because gain jitter changes
   every mode by the same factor and a moved stick changes each one by a
   different one. Measured across a +-3% hand scatter the per-mode spread
   is wildly uneven: a median of 0.4 dB, and 17.8 dB on whichever mode has
   a Bessel null nearby.

   The eight zeros below are the first eight of the ideal circular
   membrane, in frequency order, and they are mode-for-mode the ratio
   table 01-organelles already ships as `drumhead`:
       (0,1) (1,1) (2,1) (0,2) (3,1) (1,2) (4,1) (2,2)
       1.000 1.593 2.136 2.295 2.653 2.917 3.155 3.500
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
var SP_M    = [0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 1, 4, 2];
var SP_BETA = [2.404825558, 3.831705970, 5.135622302, 5.520078110, 6.380161896, 7.015586670, 7.588342435, 8.417244140];
