/* ── the galant schemata ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Robert Gjerdingen, Music in the Galant Style (2007), over the Neapolitan
   partimento tradition — Fenaroli, Durante — and the Regola dell'ottava.
   These ARE transcribed grammars with a named lineage, which is exactly why
   they belong in this file and not in a chord generator: a partimento is a
   bass with a rule for realising it, i.e. a cell plus what may be done to it,
   which is this file's definition of a tongue two centuries early. */
