  /* ── TRAITS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     What the listener asked the mix to SOUND like, folded in after the roster
     is drawn and placed. It reads only opts.traits and which roles exist, and
     it consumes no randomness, so every dice / mute / promotion identity
     holds by construction — the same argument as the register pass (§19) and
     the presence trade (RING 10). A world with no traits is byte-identical to
     one built before this existed. */
  var traitCtx = applyTraits(roster, opts.traits, style);
